---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
import Icon from "@dst/ui/Icon.astro";
import { formatDate } from "@dst/ui/date";
import { checkedOn, forum, forumDate, ticketsFrom, ticketsTo } from "../content";
import { go } from "../outbound";

const salesEnd = formatDate(forum.tickets!.salesEnd!);
---
<Layout
  title="Future World Forum Dubai tickets"
  description={`Future World Forum Dubai 2026 tickets: ${ticketsFrom} to ${ticketsTo}, sales close ${salesEnd}, refunds up to seven days before. What the price band does and doesn't tell you.`}
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Tickets</p>
    <h1>What a seat costs</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Tickets for {forumDate} are sold on Eventbrite by the organiser, in a
      band from <strong>{ticketsFrom}</strong> to <strong>{ticketsTo}</strong>.
      This site does not sell tickets and takes nothing from the sale — the
      figures here are read off the listing so you can decide before clicking.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The numbers</h2>
    <div class="figure-grid">
      <div class="figure">
        <p class="figure-label">Lowest listed</p>
        <p class="figure-value">{ticketsFrom}</p>
        <p class="figure-note">The entry tier, whatever it turns out to include</p>
      </div>
      <div class="figure">
        <p class="figure-label">Highest listed</p>
        <p class="figure-value">{ticketsTo}</p>
        <p class="figure-note">Almost certainly an exhibitor or sponsor package</p>
      </div>
      <div class="figure">
        <p class="figure-label">Sales close</p>
        <p class="figure-value">{salesEnd}</p>
        <p class="figure-note">Seven weeks before the event</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <dl class="pending">
      <div class="pending-row">
        <dt>Refunds</dt>
        <dd>{forum.tickets!.refundPolicy}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="pending-row">
        <dt>Sold by</dt>
        <dd>Eventbrite, on behalf of {forum.organizer}</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="table-note">Read from the listing on {checkedOn}. Prices on the seller's page are what count.</p>
    <p>
      <a class="button" href={go("tickets")} rel="nofollow sponsored" title="Ticket page for Future World Forum Dubai on Eventbrite">
        <Icon name="ticket" />
        Tickets on Eventbrite
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What the band means</h2>
    <p>
      A spread from under fifty dollars to over three thousand is not a
      pricing tier for the same thing. On a one-day conference and expo it
      almost always separates three products: a delegate seat at the bottom,
      a premium or group pass in the middle, and an exhibitor or sponsor
      package at the top, where the fee buys floor space rather than a chair.
    </p>
    <p>
      The listing does not spell that out, so treat the reading above as an
      inference from the shape of the price band and not as a fact about this
      event. If you are considering anything above the entry tier, ask the
      organiser in writing what the tier includes — stand size, staff passes,
      speaking slot, attendee list — before paying.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout kind="warn">
    <strong>The deadline is the thing to diarise.</strong> Sales close
    {salesEnd}, and refunds stop seven days before {forumDate}. Between those
    two dates a ticket is neither buyable nor returnable, which is a narrower
    window than most events leave.
  </Callout>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Before you pay</h2>
    <ul class="checks">
      <li><strong>Ask where it is.</strong> The listing names no venue — see <a href="/venue/" title="What is known about the venue">the venue page</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Ask what your tier includes</strong>, in writing, if you are buying above entry level.</li>
      <li><strong>Book refundable travel</strong> until the venue is confirmed.</li>
      <li><strong>Keep the Eventbrite receipt</strong> — the refund window runs from the platform, not the organiser.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the date again</strong> a week before you fly. This page is updated when the listing changes.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  th[scope="row"] { width: 12rem; color: var(--ink-muted); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .table-note { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .checks { max-width: 68ch; }
  .checks li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
</style>
